1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,142
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:02,922 --> 00:00:05,104
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:07,305 --> 00:00:08,386
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:10,547 --> 00:00:11,908
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:12,508 --> 00:00:13,809
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:14,689 --> 00:00:16,990
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:17,831 --> 00:00:20,312
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:20,412 --> 00:00:20,812
the Earth.

9
00:00:21,673 --> 00:00:23,854
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:24,695 --> 00:00:27,216
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:28,056 --> 00:00:31,098
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:31,839 --> 00:00:35,040
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,560
occur.

14
00:00:36,241 --> 00:00:37,362
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:39,444 --> 00:00:41,065
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:42,126 --> 00:00:43,347
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:44,568 --> 00:00:46,990
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:47,490
space.

19
00:00:48,651 --> 00:00:52,014
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:53,975
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:54,376 --> 00:00:56,637
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:00:58,779 --> 00:01:02,001
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:01:02,101 --> 00:01:02,661
was flat.

24
00:01:03,481 --> 00:01:07,044
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:01:07,124 --> 00:01:09,145
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:01:09,285 --> 00:01:09,905
is spherical.

27
00:01:10,706 --> 00:01:14,468
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:01:14,668 --> 00:01:17,390
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:01:17,490 --> 00:01:19,431
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:19,611 --> 00:01:21,372
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:22,153 --> 00:01:25,134
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:25,214 --> 00:01:27,156
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:27,976 --> 00:01:29,819
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:32,022 --> 00:01:33,884
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:34,885 --> 00:01:38,150
Rotation – The Earth
spins on its axis

36
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:39,171
around itself.

37
00:01:40,273 --> 00:01:43,517
Revolution – The Earth
moves around the Sun.

38
00:01:44,578 --> 00:01:45,138
Rotation.

39
00:01:47,279 --> 00:01:49,259
The movement of the Earth around its

40
00:01:49,459 --> 00:01:51,540
own axis is called rotation.

41
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,801
The earth rotates from west to east.

42
00:01:55,561 --> 00:01:58,382
It completes one full rotation in 24

43
00:01:58,462 --> 00:01:58,842
hours.

44
00:01:59,522 --> 00:02:01,703
The speed of rotation is faster at

45
00:02:01,783 --> 00:02:04,323
the equator and slower at the poles.

46
00:02:05,064 --> 00:02:07,264
The axis is tilted at an angle

47
00:02:07,364 --> 00:02:09,285
of 23.5°.

48
00:02:10,085 --> 00:02:11,905
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

49
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,526
only one half of the Earth receives

50
00:02:14,626 --> 00:02:15,687
sunlight at a time.

51
00:02:16,387 --> 00:02:18,467
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

52
00:02:18,547 --> 00:02:20,308
the Sun experience day.

53
00:02:21,008 --> 00:02:21,748
On the other hand,

54
00:02:22,228 --> 00:02:22,988
the other half,

55
00:02:23,449 --> 00:02:24,969
or the part away from the sun,

56
00:02:25,489 --> 00:02:26,669
experiences night.

57
00:02:27,470 --> 00:02:28,630
As the Earth rotates,

58
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:31,531
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

59
00:02:32,231 --> 00:02:34,852
This rotation causes day and night.

60
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:36,073
Do You Know?

61
00:02:38,216 --> 00:02:40,139
The Earth rotates at a speed of

62
00:02:40,419 --> 00:02:44,686
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

63
00:02:45,407 --> 00:02:47,350
but we don’t feel it because we’re

64
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:48,512
moving along with it!

65
00:02:49,253 --> 00:02:49,913
Revolution.

66
00:02:52,094 --> 00:02:54,454
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

67
00:02:54,654 --> 00:02:56,715
around the Sun in a fixed path

68
00:02:57,015 --> 00:02:58,015
called an orbit.

69
00:02:58,675 --> 00:03:00,815
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

70
00:03:00,895 --> 00:03:02,096
an elliptical orbit.

71
00:03:02,776 --> 00:03:04,996
It takes three hundred and sixty-five and

72
00:03:05,216 --> 00:03:08,117
one quarter days (one year) to complete

73
00:03:08,437 --> 00:03:09,217
one revolution.

74
00:03:09,877 --> 00:03:12,218
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

75
00:03:12,318 --> 00:03:13,938
the same during revolution.

76
00:03:14,658 --> 00:03:16,979
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

77
00:03:17,699 --> 00:03:19,599
The revolution of the Earth and the

78
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:22,460
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

79
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:26,320
Summer – The hemisphere
tilted towards the Sun

80
00:03:26,661 --> 00:03:27,841
experiences summer.

81
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:31,542
Winter – The hemisphere
tilted away from the

82
00:03:31,622 --> 00:03:33,342
Sun experiences winter.

83
00:03:34,022 --> 00:03:37,443
Spring – Occurs between
winter and summer when

84
00:03:37,523 --> 00:03:39,043
the temperature starts rising.

85
00:03:39,703 --> 00:03:42,944
Autumn – Occurs between
summer and winter when

86
00:03:43,024 --> 00:03:44,544
the temperature starts dropping.

87
00:03:45,464 --> 00:03:46,385
Let's Learn More.

88
00:03:48,546 --> 00:03:51,087
A day on Earth is actually 23

89
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:52,849
hours, 56 minutes,

90
00:03:53,549 --> 00:03:55,330
not exactly 24 hours,

91
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:57,651
but we round it off to 24

92
00:03:57,731 --> 00:03:59,973
hours because it’s easier to keep track

93
00:04:00,053 --> 00:04:00,493
of time.

94
00:04:01,294 --> 00:04:03,415
What is Solstice and When Does It

95
00:04:03,575 --> 00:04:03,975
Occur?

96
00:04:05,936 --> 00:04:07,216
A solstice is a day,

97
00:04:07,756 --> 00:04:09,937
when the sun shines vertically over a

98
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:13,398
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

99
00:04:13,518 --> 00:04:16,159
afternoon and the day is the longest

100
00:04:16,299 --> 00:04:17,160
in that hemisphere.

101
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,680
On the twenty-second of December,

102
00:04:20,261 --> 00:04:22,321
the rays of the sun fall directly

103
00:04:22,461 --> 00:04:23,882
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

104
00:04:24,682 --> 00:04:26,803
This is the longest day in Southern

105
00:04:26,883 --> 00:04:28,524
Hemisphere (summer season),

106
00:04:29,024 --> 00:04:30,424
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

107
00:04:30,864 --> 00:04:33,125
it is the shortest day (winter season).

108
00:04:33,785 --> 00:04:35,866
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

109
00:04:36,706 --> 00:04:38,087
On the twenty-first of June,

110
00:04:38,727 --> 00:04:41,148
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

111
00:04:41,248 --> 00:04:41,708
Cancer.

112
00:04:42,368 --> 00:04:44,509
This is the longest day in Northern

113
00:04:44,589 --> 00:04:47,590
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

114
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:50,071
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

115
00:04:50,471 --> 00:04:51,552
it is the shortest day.

116
00:04:52,352 --> 00:04:53,292
Let's Learn More.

117
00:04:55,453 --> 00:04:57,834
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

118
00:04:58,514 --> 00:05:01,075
the same reason you continue moving forward

119
00:05:01,455 --> 00:05:03,016
when you stop a bike suddenly.

120
00:05:03,776 --> 00:05:06,477
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

121
00:05:06,637 --> 00:05:08,618
friction in space to slow it down!

122
00:05:09,458 --> 00:05:11,559
What is Equinox and When Does It

123
00:05:11,719 --> 00:05:12,119
Occur?

124
00:05:14,021 --> 00:05:16,262
The sun falls directly on the equator

125
00:05:16,542 --> 00:05:17,623
two times in a year.

126
00:05:18,483 --> 00:05:20,945
During this period there is equal length

127
00:05:21,025 --> 00:05:22,886
of day and night all over the

128
00:05:22,966 --> 00:05:23,326
world.

129
00:05:23,986 --> 00:05:25,047
In Northern Hemisphere,

130
00:05:25,547 --> 00:05:27,828
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

131
00:05:28,149 --> 00:05:31,551
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

132
00:05:31,631 --> 00:05:33,071
called Autumnal Equinox.

133
00:05:34,012 --> 00:05:37,954
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

134
00:05:38,094 --> 00:05:38,574
of spring.

135
00:05:39,435 --> 00:05:43,257
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

136
00:05:43,477 --> 00:05:44,078
of autumn.

137
00:05:44,858 --> 00:05:45,319
Recall.

138
00:05:47,441 --> 00:05:48,642
The Earth's movements,

139
00:05:49,102 --> 00:05:50,904
rotation and revolution,

140
00:05:51,444 --> 00:05:53,667
have significant affects on our lives.

141
00:05:54,547 --> 00:05:56,609
Rotation causes day and night,

142
00:05:57,310 --> 00:05:59,552
while revolution leads to the change of

143
00:05:59,652 --> 00:06:00,133
seasons.

144
00:06:01,074 --> 00:06:04,037
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

145
00:06:04,137 --> 00:06:06,939
seasons, playing an essential role in our

146
00:06:07,019 --> 00:06:08,521
climate and timekeeping.

147
00:06:09,522 --> 00:06:10,303
Let's Remember.

148
00:06:12,424 --> 00:06:14,205
The Earth moves in two ways:

149
00:06:14,926 --> 00:06:16,687
rotation and revolution.

150
00:06:17,467 --> 00:06:19,428
Rotation causes day and night,

151
00:06:19,949 --> 00:06:22,010
while revolution causes seasons.

152
00:06:22,931 --> 00:06:25,753
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

153
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:28,955
hours and one revolution in three hundred

154
00:06:29,035 --> 00:06:31,076
and sixty-five and one quarter days.

155
00:06:32,037 --> 00:06:34,518
Solstices occur in June and December,

156
00:06:34,999 --> 00:06:37,260
marking the longest and shortest days.

157
00:06:38,121 --> 00:06:40,742
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

158
00:06:41,183 --> 00:06:43,124
when day and night are equal.

159
00:06:43,904 --> 00:06:44,464
Word Bank.

160
00:06:46,665 --> 00:06:49,646
Rotation – Spinning of
the Earth on its

161
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:50,226
axis.

162
00:06:51,287 --> 00:06:54,508
Revolution – Movement of
the Earth around the

163
00:06:54,588 --> 00:06:54,988
Sun.

164
00:06:55,809 --> 00:06:58,510
Orbit – The path
of the Earth around

165
00:06:58,590 --> 00:06:58,990
the Sun.

166
00:06:59,890 --> 00:07:02,331
Solstice – When the
Sun is at its

167
00:07:02,451 --> 00:07:04,612
farthest point north or south.

168
00:07:05,472 --> 00:07:08,554
Equinox – When day
and night are equal.
